    "sourceEdition": "Traditional Southern American setting, 4/4 in B minor, from the public-domain ABC folk archive; transposed here to A minor",
    "notes": "This is the traditional Aeolian setting, not the arrangement of any modern recording. The melody is pure natural minor, so every seventh degree is the flat seventh, deliberately left unraised even under the major V chord. Words are carried on the verse and refrain under their own separate traditional pd basis. The three-eighth pickup that opens the tune is kept at the end of the intro and at the end of the refrain."
  },
